// 009.3, 006.7, 009.5 (D38, #16, #44, #47): exact clock-threshold stamps on derived facts,
// `Due within d Grace g` with `?late` vs `?violated`, `Due within d After event`, and `Every p`.
Param start : Time = 0
Bool second-week Holds when Current Time - start >= 7
Bool a-day-into-it Holds when Held(second-week) For 1

Role tenant Is Tess
Role landlord Is Lou
Duty rent-due Holder tenant Claimant landlord Due within 5 Grace 3

Event notice-given
Duty cure-due Holder tenant Claimant landlord Holds when Done(notice-given) Due within 10 After notice-given

Role payer Is Daniel
Role payee Is Rosa
Act pay-period Actor payer Recipient payee Related to int Holds when True
Duty monthly-support Holder payer Claimant payee
  Every 30
  Due within 5
  Paid by pay-period
  On breach Creates support-breached
Bool support-breached
.
// 1. Jump straight from t=0 to t=9 without visiting t=7 (#16): `second-week` is stamped at 7!
+rent-due(Tess, Lou).
@ 5.
?late rent-due(Tess, Lou).
?!violated rent-due(Tess, Lou).
@ 8.
?late rent-due(Tess, Lou).
?violated rent-due(Tess, Lou).

@ 9.
?second-week.
?a-day-into-it.

// 2. `Due within 10 After notice-given`:
@ 12.
notice-given().
@ 21.
?!violated cure-due(Tess, Lou).
@ 22.
?violated cure-due(Tess, Lou).

// 3. `Every 30 Due within 5 Paid by pay-period On breach Creates support-breached` (#47):
// Period 0 (t=0) breached by t=22 -> `support-breached` holds; pay period 0, then jump to @ 32:
?support-breached.
pay-period(0).
?!monthly-support(Daniel, Rosa, 0).
@ 32.
// Period 1 arose at t=30 (stamped 30): at t=32 it holds and is NOT yet violated (32 - 30 < 5)!
?monthly-support(Daniel, Rosa, 1).
?!violated monthly-support(Daniel, Rosa, 1).
@ 35.
?violated monthly-support(Daniel, Rosa, 1).
